<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train the compression and alignment module on 1M images from Cambrian <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>.
For downstream fine-tuning, we use FineVision <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wiedmann et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, Visual Spatial Reasoning (VSR) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and PathVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2020</a>)</cite> for general and domain-specific understanding.
Detailed data composition and preprocessing are provided in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Experimental Details ‣ What Generation Knows: Unlocking Fine-Grained Understanding in Unified Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models and Training.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We experiment on three UMMs, BAGEL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, Janus-Pro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025c</a>)</cite>, and Lance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2026</a>)</cite>.
During compression and alignment, we freeze the native pathways and optimize the Encoder, Decoder, and prediction heads.
During task-conditioned fine-tuning, we optimize the injection modules and understanding-pathway LoRA adapters, with the compression Encoder later unfrozen for joint optimization.
Training configurations and hyperparameters are provided in
Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Experimental Details ‣ What Generation Knows: Unlocking Fine-Grained Understanding in Unified Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For general fine-grained visual understanding, we evaluate on VStar-Bench, OmniSpatial, and MMVP, covering fine-grained visual perception and spatial understanding.
For domain-specific evaluation, we report results on VSR-Bench and PathVQA.
We compare against the Base model and SFT baselines trained on the same data.
Evaluation details are provided in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Experimental Details ‣ What Generation Knows: Unlocking Fine-Grained Understanding in Unified Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
