<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Resolution Stability</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test whether the generation-side advantage depends on input scale, we repeat the same image preprocessing, representation extraction, common-grid alignment, and control-correction procedures at input resolutions of 128, 256, and 512. At each resolution, the long edge is first reduced to the target resolution and then restored to the model input size by interpolation.
We report the control-corrected generation–understanding response gap for all six models, four domains, and three input resolutions in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.4 Resolution Stability ‣ Appendix A Details of Representation Sensitivity Analysis ‣ What Generation Knows: Unlocking Fine-Grained Understanding in Unified Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
