<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Compression and Alignment</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Stage 1, we freeze the native understanding and generation pathways of the unified multimodal model and optimize only the GToken Encoder, Decoder, and their prediction heads.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The GToken Encoder–Decoder adopts a symmetric six-layer Transformer architecture with a hidden size of 1024, 8 attention heads, and a 4096-dimensional FFN, together with 2D RoPE for spatial position encoding. The Encoder first projects the generation representation to 1024 dimensions and concatenates it with 256 learnable queries. Joint self-attention with spatial positional encoding then aggregates the generation information. The query outputs are subsequently projected to the hidden dimension of the corresponding understanding-pathway tokens, forming a fixed-length generation memory <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. The dimensions of <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> for BAGEL, Janus-Pro, and Lance are 3584, 4096, and 2048, respectively. The Decoder projects <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> back to 1024 dimensions, concatenates it with reconstruction queries arranged according to the source grid, and reconstructs the original generation representation through joint self-attention and a linear prediction head.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For spatial binding, we construct <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}^{\mathrm{bind}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>bind</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}^{\mathrm{bind}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the
<math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\times 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\times 16</annotation></semantics></math> grid of the 256 <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. For BAGEL and Lance,
<math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}^{\mathrm{bind}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>bind</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}^{\mathrm{bind}}</annotation></semantics></math> is formed by concatenating the corresponding
<math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> region of the <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> grid obtained from the native
generation latent. For Janus-Pro, it is obtained by adaptively average-pooling
the native <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24\times 24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24\times 24</annotation></semantics></math> grid to <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\times 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\times 16</annotation></semantics></math>. Each <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> predicts the
<math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}^{\mathrm{bind}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>bind</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}^{\mathrm{bind}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the same spatial location, using a target-energy-
normalized mean squared error.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Compression and Alignment ‣ What Generation Knows: Unlocking Fine-Grained Understanding in Unified Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> visualizes reconstructions on held-out images. Each case compares the original image, the reconstruction obtained by directly decoding the native generation-side representation (VAE upper bound), and the reconstruction obtained from the compressed <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2610.23987v1/figures/stage1_visualization.png" id="A2.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/218;" width="548" height="218" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>
<span id="A2.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 1 reconstruction visualization.</span>
Each case compares the original image, the VAE upper bound obtained by decoding the native generation representation, and the reconstruction from the compressed <math id="A2.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens.
</figcaption>
