<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Task-Conditioned Injection and Fine-Tuning</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the initial stage of Stage 2, we freeze the native visual encoders, the Stage 1 GToken Encoder–Decoder, and the LLM backbone, and optimize only the projector, the internal cross-attention injection modules, and the LoRA modules in the understanding pathway. During the latter half of training, we unfreeze the GToken Encoder and jointly optimize it with the projector, internal injection modules, and LoRA modules. The native visual encoders remain frozen throughout training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The projector maps the <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens to the corresponding understanding width and uses the same positional encoding scheme as the native understanding-side visual tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Each internal attention injection block uses the current-layer text hidden states in the understanding pathway as queries and projects the queries, keys, and values into a 1024-dimensional, 16-head attention space. The retrieved features are passed through an output projection and residually written back to the text hidden states. The output projection is zero-initialized so that the injection modules do not alter the original understanding pathway at the beginning of training. The LoRA rank and alpha are both set to 16.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The overall training objective consists of answer supervision on matched samples, a CE-space pairwise DPO objective between matched and mismatched generation memories, and a KL regularizer on the shuffle-<math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\lambda_{\mathrm{CE}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CE}}^{\mathrm{real}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{DPO}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL}}(t)\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>CE</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CE</mi><mi>real</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>shuffle</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\lambda_{\mathrm{CE}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CE}}^{\mathrm{real}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{DPO}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL}}(t)\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CE}}^{\mathrm{real}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CE</mi><mi>real</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CE}}^{\mathrm{real}}</annotation></semantics></math> provides answer supervision with the matched <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens; <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> compares answer CE under matched and mismatched generation memories to encourage the use of sample-relevant generation information; and <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>shuffle</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}</annotation></semantics></math> constrains the effect of mismatched <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens on the original output distribution. In the default configuration, <math id="A3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{CE}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>CE</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{CE}}=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{DPO}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{DPO}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the DPO temperature is <math id="A3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. The positive and negative DPO branches are assigned gradient weights <math id="A3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{+}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{+}=4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{-}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{-}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, and the norm of the negative gradient is capped at <math id="A3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math> times the norm of the positive gradient. The base weight of the shuffle-<math id="A3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> KL loss is <math id="A3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>; its effective coefficient <math id="A3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> remains at <math id="A3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> initially, then linearly decays to <math id="A3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math>, briefly remains at <math id="A3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math>, and finally linearly decays to <math id="A3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> over the 5,000 optimizer steps.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For each training sample <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the question and answer, <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the native understanding representation, and <math id="A3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding <math id="A3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. We construct the following three branches:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The real/positive branch uses <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},U_{i},G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},U_{i},G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is matched to the current sample, and computes answer-token CE under teacher forcing with the answer <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The shuffle-<math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch uses <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},U_{i},G_{\pi(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},U_{i},G_{\pi(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>, replacing only the generation memory with a donor memory while retaining the current sample’s question, answer, and understanding representation. Donors are selected deterministically by a half-manifest offset: for a manifest containing an even number <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> of samples, <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(i)=(i+N/2)\bmod N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(i)=(i+N/2)\bmod N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reference branch does not receive the <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens and disables the generation-memory injection modules and understanding-pathway LoRA. It uses the frozen native model to compute the reference distribution conditioned on <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},U_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},U_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q_{i},U_{i},y_{i,&lt;t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q_{i},U_{i},y_{i,&lt;t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This branch does not participate in backpropagation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CE loss.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of answer-token positions for sample <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}=|\mathcal{T}_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}=|\mathcal{T}_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>. In the real/positive branch, the model receives the matched <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and computes the negative log-likelihood of the correct answer tokens:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{i}^{+}=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\log p_{\theta}\left(y_{i,t}\mid q_{i},U_{i},G_{i},y_{i,&lt;t}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{+}=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\log p_{\theta}\left(y_{i,t}\mid q_{i},U_{i},G_{i},y_{i,&lt;t}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}^{+}=\frac{s_{i}^{+}}{n_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}^{+}=\frac{s_{i}^{+}}{n_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The real-pair CE loss is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CE}}^{\mathrm{real}}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\ell_{i}^{+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CE</mi><mi>real</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CE}}^{\mathrm{real}}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\ell_{i}^{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">CE-space pairwise DPO objective.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To encourage the model to use the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens matched to the current sample, we replace <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\pi(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\pi(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> from another image to construct the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch. This branch keeps <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged and replaces only the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{i}^{-}=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\log p_{\theta}\left(y_{i,t}\mid q_{i},U_{i},G_{\pi(i)},y_{i,&lt;t}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{-}=-\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}\log p_{\theta}\left(y_{i,t}\mid q_{i},U_{i},G_{\pi(i)},y_{i,&lt;t}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}^{-}=\frac{s_{i}^{-}}{n_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}^{-}=\frac{s_{i}^{-}}{n_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the matched <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the mismatched <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\pi(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\pi(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The CE-space pairwise DPO objective requires the matched <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens to achieve a lower answer CE than the mismatched memory:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\operatorname{softplus}\left[-\beta\left(\ell_{i}^{-}-\ell_{i}^{+}\right)\right],\qquad\beta=0.1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>DPO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>softplus</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO}}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\operatorname{softplus}\left[-\beta\left(\ell_{i}^{-}-\ell_{i}^{+}\right)\right],\qquad\beta=0.1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> KL loss.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute an answer-token-level forward KL only on the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch. The reference branch disables the generation-memory injection modules and understanding-pathway LoRA and uses the frozen native model conditioned on <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate the reference distribution:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{ref},i,t}=p_{\mathrm{ref}}\left(\cdot\mid q_{i},U_{i},y_{i,&lt;t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{ref},i,t}=p_{\mathrm{ref}}\left(\cdot\mid q_{i},U_{i},y_{i,&lt;t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The current model’s output distribution on the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta,i,t}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}=p_{\theta}\left(\cdot\mid q_{i},U_{i},G_{\pi(i)},y_{i,&lt;t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>shuffle</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta,i,t}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}=p_{\theta}\left(\cdot\mid q_{i},U_{i},G_{\pi(i)},y_{i,&lt;t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> KL loss is therefore defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\frac{1}{n_{i}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(p_{\mathrm{ref},i,t}\;\middle\|\;p_{\theta,i,t}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi><mi>shuffle</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>shuffle</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\frac{1}{n_{i}}\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}_{i}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\left(p_{\mathrm{ref},i,t}\;\middle\|\;p_{\theta,i,t}^{\mathrm{shuffle}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The reference distribution is detached from the computational graph, and the reference branch is not updated. This term limits the output-distribution shift caused by mismatched <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens and prevents the model from enlarging the positive–negative CE gap merely by degrading the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gradient decomposition.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During training, we separately compute the gradients from the real/positive branch and the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch. The real/positive gradient contains the answer-CE gradient and the positive DPO gradient, while the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> branch produces the negative DPO gradient. The positive and negative DPO gradients are combined with weights of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4:1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4:1</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The global norm of the negative gradient is then capped at <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math> times that of the real/positive gradient, after which it is added to the real/positive gradient and the shuffle-<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> KL gradient. Finally, the combined gradient is clipped to a maximum global norm of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Understanding-representation masking.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To reduce reliance on the native understanding pathway during early training, we mask the complete understanding representation <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each sample with probability <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{U}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{U}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, while keeping the corresponding generation memory <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, question, and answer unchanged.
For the formal training run with 5,000 optimizer steps, the mask probability follows the schedule:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{U}(t)=\begin{cases}0.8,&amp;0&lt;t\leq 1250,\\
0.5,&amp;1250&lt;t\leq 2500,\\
0.2,&amp;2500&lt;t\leq 3750,\\
0,&amp;3750&lt;t\leq 5000.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.8</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1250</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1250</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2500</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>2500</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3750</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>3750</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5000</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{U}(t)=\begin{cases}0.8,&amp;0&lt;t\leq 1250,\\
0.5,&amp;1250&lt;t\leq 2500,\\
0.2,&amp;2500&lt;t\leq 3750,\\
0,&amp;3750&lt;t\leq 5000.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the model relies more heavily on the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> tokens in the early stages and gradually restores the complete understanding representation, allowing the two pathways to cooperate in the later stages of training.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Data</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The compression and alignment stage uses 1M images sampled with stratification from Cambrian. For task-conditioned fine-tuning, we select 1,344,016 samples with relevance scores of at least 3 from the non-text-only subset of FineVision. VSR-Bench uses 7,680 training samples from its official random split and 2,195 samples from its official test split. For the medical-domain experiments, we use 19,654 training samples and 6,719 test samples from the official PathVQA splits.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Representative examples from the three datasets are shown below. They illustrate fine-grained multi-object reasoning in FineVision, local spatial-relation recognition in VSR-Bench, and pathological visual question answering in PathVQA.</p>
